  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">I1: introducing a Param([string]$TenantId = 'a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-1234567890ab') into any .ps1 under scripts/ causes I1 test to fail with file:line.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">I2: introducing a Search*Async call in src/server/** with a Filter that lacks "tenantId eq " causes I2 test to fail with file:line.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">I3: introducing a Container.ReadItemAsync call in src/server/** without an explicit PartitionKey argument causes I3 test to fail with file:line; existing [AllowCrossPartitionScan]-annotated call sites do NOT fail.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">I4: introducing a string literal "b!ABCD..." in src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/** causes I4 test to fail with file:line.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">I5: introducing a Graph client construction with `.default` scope and no explicit tenantId parameter causes I5 test to fail with file:line.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All 5 tests PASS against the current codebase (post-1834b77bc script fix); any pre-existing violation is filed as a task-065 finding.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test suite runtime &lt;10s in CI (verified locally via `dotnet test --logger console` timing).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0; zero analyzer warnings.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

